  "feature1": {
    "prompt": "The Requests library currently fails to process requests with a binary payload because it applies an unnecessary conversion using to_native_string. This leads to errors when binary data is submitted, even though the same request worked in version 2.8.1. The issue was originally introduced as noted in https://github.com/kennethreitz/requests/issues/2844. The fix must ensure that binary data is not altered by an improper conversion, so that payloads remain intact.",
    "hint_texts": "This feature focuses on correcting the treatment of binary data during parameter encoding. Developers should remove the call to to_native_string inside the encoding logic so that for data types such as str or bytes, the value is returned as-is. This change prevents unnecessary conversion of binary payloads. Implementation efforts should concentrate on modifying the _encode_params function in the Requests source.",
    "entrypoint": "File: requests/models.py \u2013 In the _encode_params function, remove the invocation of to_native_string for objects that are already strings or bytes and return the data unchanged.",
    "tests": {
      "FAIL_TO_PASS": "",
      "PASS_TO_PASS": "test_requests.py::TestRequests::test_params_bytes_are_encoded"
    }
  },
  "feature2": {
    "prompt": "The Requests library fails when sending PUT requests with a binary payload due to an incorrect invocation of to_native_string. In the provided example, a PUT request using binary encoded data fails in version 2.9 even though it worked in version 2.8.1. The problem is linked to an unnecessary conversion step as documented at https://github.com/kennethreitz/requests/issues/2844. The remedy should reestablish proper handling for binary payloads so that they are processed correctly without error.",
    "hint_texts": "This feature targets the URL preparation phase where request parameters are processed. Developers are expected to add a conditional check so that if the parameters are provided as a string or bytes, they are converted with to_native_string only when needed. This ensures that the payload integrity is maintained while still applying necessary encoding. The implementation should be done in the prepare_url method and coordinated with the changes in parameter encoding.",
    "entrypoint": "File: requests/models.py \u2013 In the prepare_url method (around line 385), insert a check that detects if params is a string or bytes, and if so, convert it using to_native_string before the parameters are encoded.",
